Track 2: "Are We Running The Last Freight South?"
- Story & Context: Recorded in the crawlspace behind Dispatch Depot B, this confessional track was written by cellist and former seed courier Tariq Danvers after he spent thirty hours trapped in an unheated passenger carriage during an Arctic blizzard. Shivering against the damp wool of his overcoat and clutching an uncataloged tin of Nigerian sorghum grains he had promised to protect, Danvers tracked his cello ostinato through a battery-operated preamp while weeping softly between takes. The emotional breakdown peaked when chanter Nia Beckford broke into the carriage to deliver the hook directly into Danvers's instrument pickup, whispering through chattering teeth: "Tell the dispatcher we left the baggage and brought the blood." The track became notorious across the archipelago for its gut-wrenching contrast between high-speed dancehall skanks and the tragic, slow-bleeding weight of Danvers’s solo contrabass.
