Track 3: Wahala Pon Di Cold Track
- Story & Context: The final legend of the EP recounts the night the Longyearbyen municipal council attempted to clear the railway sidings of sound-system gear by sending an automated maintenance snowplow down the line. Instead of retreating, Adeyemi assembled twenty-four string players across the loading dock while Baptiste hammered an unhinged Afrobeat counter-melody onto twin chromatic steel drums that rattled the permafrost down to the bedrock vaults. The intense, sulfur-tinged smell of overworked plow belts filled the siding until the vehicle’s computerized emergency brakes tripped from the sheer low-frequency sound pressure radiating through the concrete floor. The crew celebrated the mechanical surrender by looping the automated warning buzzer as a rhythm track, chanting the victory refrain: "Iron bow down when the root start shake!"
